Basic Dropdown Questions
	1. How do you select a value from a dropdown in Selenium using Java?
		○ Use the Select class from org.openqa.selenium.support.ui.Select:
WebElement dropdown = driver.findElement(By.id("dropdownId"));
Select select = new Select(dropdown);
select.selectByVisibleText("Option 1");
	2. What are the different ways to select an option from a dropdown?
		○ selectByVisibleText("Text")
		○ selectByValue("value")
		○ selectByIndex(index)
	3. How to deselect options from a dropdown?
		○ Only applicable to multi-select dropdowns:
select.deselectByVisibleText("Option 1");
select.deselectAll();
Intermediate/Scenario-Based Questions
	1. How do you check if a dropdown allows multiple selections?
Select select = new Select(driver.findElement(By.id("multiSelect")));
System.out.println("Is multiple: " + select.isMultiple());
	2. How do you get all selected options from a multi-select dropdown?
List<WebElement> selectedOptions = select.getAllSelectedOptions();
for (WebElement option : selectedOptions) {
    System.out.println(option.getText());
}
	3. How do you get all options available in a dropdown?
List<WebElement> allOptions = select.getOptions();
for (WebElement option : allOptions) {
    System.out.println(option.getText());
}
	4. How do you select multiple values in a multi-select dropdown?
select.selectByIndex(0);
select.selectByValue("value2");
select.selectByVisibleText("Option 3");

🔹 Advanced/Custom Dropdown Questions
	1. How do you handle custom-styled dropdowns (not using <select> tag)?
		○ You must interact with the dropdown like regular elements:
driver.findElement(By.id("customDropdown")).click();  // Open dropdown
driver.findElement(By.xpath("//li[text()='Option 2']")).click();  // Select option
	2. What challenges do you face with dynamic/custom dropdowns?
		○ No <select> tag
		○ Options not in DOM until dropdown is clicked
		○ Requires explicit waits
		○ May require JavaScript scrolling or visibility checks
	3. How do you select a dropdown option using JavaScriptExecutor?
JavascriptExecutor js = (JavascriptExecutor) driver;
js.executeScript("document.getElementById('dropdownId').value = 'optionValue';");

🔍 Common Issues and Their Fixes
	• StaleElementReferenceException: Re-fetch the dropdown element before selecting.
	• ElementNotInteractableException: Use explicit wait or scroll into view before clicking.
	• Dropdown not showing options: Click to open it before attempting selection.
